      "category": "engine",
      "title": "Top-End Engine Ticking from Hydraulic Lash Adjusters (LSY 2.0T)",
      "description": "2025-2026 Envisions with the 2.0L turbo LSY four-cylinder develop an audible ticking noise from the top of the engine. Caused by manufacturing debris inside the Stationary Hydraulic Lash Adjusters (SHLAs) preventing proper oil pumping, leaving valvetrain clearance unmaintained. GM PIP6101A (Feb 2026) supersedes PIP6061.",
      "solution": "Per PIP6101A, dealer removes camshaft carrier, inspects for soft SHLAs, and replaces failed lash adjusters AND their matched rocker arms. Covered under powertrain warranty - do not let dealer dismiss as normal direct-injection noise.",
      "severity": "high",
      "confidence": "high",
      "symptoms": [
        "sewing-machine ticking from valve cover area",
        "ticking worst at cold start and idle",
        "noise may persist when warm",
        "no power loss but audible from outside"
      ],
